WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.010
So Terry, what was your aha moment?

2
00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:06.690
I know that you said you didn't want to lose her,

3
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.956
but what was it for you?

4
00:00:08.956 --> 00:00:10.310
I'm going to be perfectly honest here,

5
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.920
when the marriage was over, I was like, okay, that's it.

6
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.410
Then I'm done.

7
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:20.410
And, but a little voice told me that it was everyone else,

8
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.440
everyone else was my issue.

9
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:26.840
And it changed when it really really cracked the egg

10
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.740
that said, this is me,

11
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.090
and I called a friend and he was my counselor and my pastor

12
00:00:34.654 --> 00:00:35.784
and he said Terry,

13
00:00:35.784 --> 00:00:37.230 line:15%
I can't tell you you're going to get your wife back,

14
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.330 line:15%
your wife is probably gone forever,

15
00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.860 line:15%
but you need to get better for you.

16
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.210 line:15%
Now, you got to understand,

17
00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.470 line:15%
for a man that was a watershed moment,

18
00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:48.240 line:15%
for me, I always did good things to get,

19
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.543 line:15%
you know, to get cookies, so to speak,

20
00:00:51.543 --> 00:00:53.480 line:15%
you always, you work out so you can look like this,

21
00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:56.160 line:15%
you do nice things, so you can get sex.

22
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.360 line:15%
You go to work so you can get money.

23
00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.890 line:15%
Wait a minute.

24
00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.540 line:15%
So you can get the girl.

25
00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.960
You know, just actually improving myself just to improve.

26
00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.800
That was like, wait a minute, he said, hey man,

27
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:09.670
this is about you,

28
00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.270
'cause you probably going to be alone and you still,

29
00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.450
are going to be stuck in your problem.

30
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:15.740
And I realized, listen,

31
00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:18.500
I didn't even go to rehab to get her back.

32
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.310
But what happened was while I was fixing myself,

33
00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:27.550
we reunited and it just, it became a,

34
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.850
now it could have went the other way,

35
00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.720
that's still Rebecca's choice,

36
00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.000
it was always Rebecca's choice

37
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.270
whether she wanted to be here or not.

38
00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:36.533
So.

39
00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:38.320
Yes, and there were many times Drew that,

40
00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.840
hey I kept plane tickets in my hand,

41
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.960
but I'm thankful I was laying in bed last night,

42
00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.960
playing the song I love called "Grateful".

43
00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.560
And all I was thinking was how grateful I am

44
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.873
that I still have Terry.

45
00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.364
I mean.

46
00:01:55.364 --> 00:01:58.790
(audience applauding)

47
00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:01.910
I really appreciate this conversation,

48
00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:06.650
but you have your children, this is all out there,

49
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.210
where do they fall into that now that

50
00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.720
the cat's out of the bag?

51
00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.420
Yes, well, you know, part of our counseling

52
00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.450
and one of the things that our counselors told us to do

53
00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.160
was to actually talk to each one of our kids

54
00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.430
and explain it at their level.

55
00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.734
And we want to make sure that they knew

56
00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.230
that this was not about them,

57
00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.300
this was not their issue,

58
00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.860
this is something a daddy and mommy are working through.

59
00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.070
Right and this is a 12-step model

60
00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.140
that's used with sex addiction.

61
00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.740
So it deals with, you know,

62
00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:39.553
talking to the victims of your behavior,

63
00:02:39.553 --> 00:02:40.386
and that included our children.

64
00:02:40.386 --> 00:02:41.650
Yeah. - Yeah.

65
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.300
Okay, on a last note

66
00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.250
I just want to say, you guys have brought

67
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:52.030
a lot of joy and levity and honesty in all of this,

68
00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:53.890
and how do you guys laugh,

69
00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:57.180
how do you guys just kick all the bags, lighten up,

70
00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.570
keep it real, have a good time,

71
00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.503
how do you do it?

72
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.250
Well, he's a bag of jokes every single day.

73
00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.300
My husband brings the fun

74
00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.990
and I bring the structure, I always say.

75
00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:13.400
We joke a lot, we make fun of each other.

76
00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.480
Generally we just like each other.

77
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.020
And I even said to him, I said,

78
00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.940
even if you left me and married someone else,

79
00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.880
I'd still be your best friend,

80
00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.400
because I know you better than anyone else.

81
00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.540
Now, she's not getting everything I worked for though,

82
00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.373
it's not fair.

83
00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.490
That's the humor I'm talking about,

84
00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:35.660
and we all need it to survive.

85
00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:40.660
Terry and Rebecca, I am so grateful for this conversation,

86
00:03:42.441 --> 00:03:45.290
and I applaud your guys's choice.

87
00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.640 line:15%
And I just think you're awesome,

88
00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.950 line:15%
thank you so much, Rebecca and Terry,

89
00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.237 line:15%
Wow, thank you so much

